AWS-019 — Workflow Conformance

Document ID: AWS-019
Title: Workflow Conformance
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Workflow Conformance Model (CWCFM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Workflow Conformance Model establishes the principles, capability profiles, testing procedures, certification requirements, interoperability validation, and governance mechanisms required to determine whether workflow implementations conform to the Atlas Workflow Specification.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Workflow conformance architecture
Capability profiles
Conformance levels
Interoperability testing
Certification
Conformance declarations
Validation
Governance

This specification applies to every implementation claiming compliance with Atlas Workflow Specifications.

3. Canonical Definition

Workflow Conformance is the demonstrable implementation of mandatory Atlas Workflow Specification requirements, verified through objective testing, evidence, and independent assessment.

Conformance evaluates implementations.

It SHALL NOT redefine workflow semantics.

4. Objectives

The Workflow Conformance Model SHALL:

Ensure implementation consistency.
Enable interoperability.
Support certification.
Preserve workflow semantics.
Support independent implementations.
Enable ecosystem compatibility.
Maintain governance.
Support continuous evolution.
5. Conformance Principles

Every Workflow Conformance assessment SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Specification Fidelity

Implementations SHALL preserve canonical AWS semantics.

Objective Verification

Conformance SHALL be demonstrated through objective evidence.

Repeatability

Equivalent implementations SHALL produce equivalent conformance outcomes.

Interoperability

Independent implementations SHALL exchange workflow artifacts without semantic loss.

Transparency

Every conformance declaration SHALL explicitly identify implemented capabilities.

Governance

Conformance SHALL remain subject to Atlas governance.

6. Conformance Subjects

Atlas recognizes the following conformance subjects.

Subject	Description
Workflow Engine	Runtime execution engine
Workflow Orchestrator	Multi-workflow coordinator
Workflow Repository	Artifact storage
Workflow Registry	Artifact discovery
Monitoring Platform	Workflow observability
AI Execution Agent	Autonomous workflow participant
Development Tool	Workflow authoring environment
Organization	Operational implementation

Additional subjects MAY be defined through future specifications.

7. Capability Profiles

Atlas defines canonical capability profiles.

Profile	Description
Core Execution	Execute Workflow Definitions
Orchestration	Coordinate workflows
Monitoring	Observe execution
Governance	Apply workflow governance
Federation	Cross-organization execution
Optimization	Continuous improvement
Distribution	Workflow deployment
Audit	Execution assurance

Profiles SHALL declare supported capabilities.

8. Conformance Levels

Atlas defines the following conformance levels.

Level	Description
Level 1	Core workflow execution
Level 2	Governed workflow execution
Level 3	Enterprise orchestration
Level 4	Federated execution
Level 5	Autonomous AI-native execution

Higher levels SHALL include lower-level capabilities unless explicitly exempted.

9. Conformance Testing

Every conformance assessment SHALL evaluate:

Workflow execution
State transitions
Event generation
Policy enforcement
Interface compatibility
Orchestration behavior
Monitoring capabilities
Audit evidence

Testing SHALL be reproducible.

10. Interoperability Validation

Atlas implementations SHALL validate interoperability for:

Workflow Definitions
Workflow Interfaces
Workflow Packages
Canonical Events
Execution Contexts
Workflow Telemetry
Federation exchanges

Validation SHALL preserve canonical semantics.

11. Certification

Certification SHALL define:

Certification authority
Certified implementation
Capability profile
Conformance level
Certification period
Applicable specification versions
Certification evidence

Certification SHALL remain independently verifiable.

12. Declaration of Conformity

Every implementation MAY publish a Declaration of Conformity including:

Organization
Product name
Product version
Supported AWS specifications
Capability profiles
Conformance level
Certification reference
Known limitations

Declarations SHALL be digitally signed where required.

