14. Conformance Governance

Every conformance program SHALL define:

Certification authority
Assessment authority
Appeal process
Suspension criteria
Revocation criteria
Renewal process
Audit requirements

Governance SHALL remain independently auditable.

15. Conformance Quality

Every conformance assessment SHALL satisfy:

Correctness
Objectivity
Repeatability
Explainability
Traceability
Auditability
Transparency
Interoperability

Quality SHALL be continuously evaluated.

16. Conformance Artifacts

Atlas recognizes the following conformance artifacts.

Artifact	Description
Test Suite	Standardized verification tests
Test Report	Assessment results
Certification Record	Official certification
Declaration of Conformity	Public implementation statement
Capability Profile	Supported features
Compliance Evidence	Supporting documentation

Artifacts SHALL remain versioned.

17. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

AI-assisted certification.
Continuous conformance monitoring.
Machine-verifiable conformance proofs.
Federated certification authorities.
Automated interoperability testing.
Digital certification credentials.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical conformance semantics.

